## 3. Workspace Detection

### The `workspaceRoot` getter (`bridge-handler.ts:241-243`):

```typescript
private get workspaceRoot(): string | null {
  return vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders?.[0]?.uri.fsPath ?? null;
}
```

This accesses `vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders[0]` — the **first workspace folder**.

### The `getWorkDir` method (`bridge-handler.ts:245-247`):

```typescript
private getWorkDir(webviewId: string): string | null {
  return this.customWorkDirs.get(webviewId) ?? this.workspaceRoot;
}
```

**Priority:** Custom overridden dir → workspace root → null.

### Custom workDir override (`session.handler.ts:219-229`):

```typescript
[Methods.SetWorkDir]: async (params: { workDir: string | null }, ctx) => {
  if (!ctx.workspaceRoot) return { ok: false };
  const target = params.workDir;
  if (target && target !== ctx.workspaceRoot && !target.startsWith(ctx.workspaceRoot + path.sep)) {
    return { ok: false };
  }
  ctx.setCustomWorkDir(target);
  return { ok: true, workDir: target || ctx.workspaceRoot };
},
```

Users can override workDir to subdirectories of the workspace root via the `BrowseWorkDir` method.

### `setCustomWorkDir` triggers session reset (`bridge-handler.ts:249-267`):

```typescript
setCustomWorkDir(webviewId: string, workDir: string | null): void {
  if (workDir && workDir !== this.workspaceRoot) {
    this.customWorkDirs.set(webviewId, workDir);
  } else {
    this.customWorkDirs.delete(webviewId);
  }
  // Close ALL sessions when workDir changes
  this.sessions.get(webviewId)?.close();
  this.sessions.delete(webviewId);
  this.turns.delete(webviewId);
  const doKey = `${webviewId}:do`;
  this.sessions.get(doKey)?.close();
  this.sessions.delete(doKey);
  this.turns.delete(doKey);
  this.fileManager.clearTracked(webviewId);
  this.fileManager.clearTracked(doKey);
}
```

### The `checkWorkspace` handler (`workspace.handler.ts:10-16`):

```typescript
const checkWorkspace: Handler<void, WorkspaceStatus> = async (_, ctx) => {
  return {
    hasWorkspace: ctx.workDir !== null,
    path: ctx.workDir ?? undefined,
    workspaceRoot: ctx.workspaceRoot ?? undefined,
  };
};
```

This is called by the webview on startup to determine if a workspace is open.

